{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All fixes are pushed to PR #3 as a second commit (fast-forward, no force). Summary of what changed and what I verified:\n\n**Format fixes in `src/targets/opencode.ts`** — now validated against opencode 1.18.5 end-to-end:\n- Tool `state` writes all six required keys (`status`/`input`/`output`/`title`/`metadata`/`time`). A tool-bearing conversation now imports; before, it died on the first one.\n- Tool calls are paired with their results up front, so the real recorded output rides in `state.output` instead of a placeholder plus a duplicate loose text copy.\n- The import notice is backdated ahead of history — opencode orders by `time.created`, so the old `now` stamp sorted it last with a `QUEUED` badge. Verified in a pty capture that it now renders first and the badge is gone.\n- `parentID` follows the real prompt→replies tree (users unparented, assistants pointing at their prompting message).\n- `projectID` is looked up via `opencode debug scrap`; verified the session now lists from the repo only, not from every directory. Falls back to `global` with an explicit note.\n- Source model id propagated per the fabrication contract; `replayReasoning` honored (folds to `[visible thinking]` when off).\n- Failed imports delete the truncated session they leave behind and raise `FabricationUnsupportedError`, so resume degrades to bootstrap instead of throwing. Lineage records the id opencode actually stored.\n\n**Shim removed.** It intercepted `opencode -s <id>`, dropped the id, and re-entered itself through PATH. opencode has no argument-free picker invocation to interpose on, so the honest fix is no shim — documented in the design doc.\n\n**Supporting work:** `docs/specs/opencode-session-format.md` (205 lines, with the verification log and an explicit Unknowns section), an opencode row in the drift check, opencode wired into `smoke:interactive` — including deleting its own session, since unlike the file-based targets it mutates a shared DB — and 12 payload-shape tests, one per defect.\n\nChecks I ran: `npm test` 88/88 pass; `npm run smoke:interactive all` passes for all three targets (markers rendered in each real TUI); drift check reports OpenCode OK against 1.18.11.\n\nThree things to know:\n- **Live continuation is still unverified.** `opencode run -s` couldn't complete — your local DS4 gateway errored on a *fresh native* session too (`metal resumed prefill failed`), so it wasn't attributable to the adapter. History presence and rendering are verified; I logged this as an open unknown in the spec rather than papering over it.\n- On resume opencode toasts `Model turnbridge/<model> is not valid` and falls back to your configured model. That's the warn-once behavior your own fabrication contract prescribes, so I left it and documented it.\n- The drift check also reports **Codex DRIFT** (0.146.0 vs pinned 0.144/0.145). Pre-existing, unrelated to this PR.\n\nYour local `feature/opencode-target` is now one commit behind the remote — `git pull` before you touch it. I cleaned up every session my testing created; only your original \"Turnbridge opencode support check\" remains.\n\nresult: PR #3 fixed and pushed — tool-call fabrication now works against opencode 1.18.5, 9 further format/robustness defects corrected, shim removed, format spec + 12 tests added; 88/88 tests and all three interactive smoke targets pass.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","dirty_fingerprint":"cf8b9e3c1e47cd671f179e23127d98edb70689fbf4ed08f9960baec974f11cfc","head":"f4b7c5c1d0ef7049f74d97ba083576c1f09a936e","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-d0e34a6f8d4dc68e6e6732f51a45acfc222f83665aa2dd7d4d2b4dac85b903a9","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","source":"claude-c