{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Yes — and it's the one check I can't do for you. Here's the honest split.\n\n**What's already verified without you:** import succeeds for tool-bearing conversations, the notice sorts first with no `QUEUED` badge, the session is scoped to the right project, markers reach the terminal in the right order, 88 unit tests, and all three targets pass the automated pty smoke.\n\n**What needs your eyes:**\n\n1. **The screen actually looking right.** Your own smoke script makes this point — stripped pty captures can't prove the render was clean, and the Codex empty-scrollback bug was exactly that failure mode. My capture proves the strings arrived, not that the layout held.\n2. **Live continuation.** Still unverified: your DS4 gateway was erroring on a *native* session too (`metal resumed prefill failed`), so I couldn't attribute anything. Sending one prompt into a bridged session is the only way to confirm the model reads the imported history.\n\n```sh\nnpm run build && node scripts/smoke-interactive.mjs opencode --manual\n```\n\nThat prints a `cd … && opencode -s ses_tb_…` line to run in a normal terminal, plus a checklist. Run it outside an agent session.\n\nTwo things I changed while preparing that recommendation, both pushed:\n\n- **The fixture had no tool call.** Structured tool history was never exercised in a real TUI for *any* target — which is precisely how this adapter shipped unable to import a conversation containing one. It now seeds a paired `tool_use`/`tool_result` with its own marker. All three targets still pass.\n- **The checklist was written for the file-based targets.** It told you to look for `[visible thinking]` text, which on opencode is a collapsed `Thought` part. It also now tells you the `Read` row must be *expanded* to see its output — Claude Code and opencode both collapse tool rows, so I'd have sent you hunting for text that isn't on screen by default. I kept the automated pass criterion on the two text markers rath